{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T14:56:07.739Z","stream":"U-17UN402ICR95C-567971","seq":1,"source":"pipeline","kind":"run-started","labels":{"run_id":"orchestrator-gate-fix-findings-2"},"payload":{"plan":{"schema_version":3,"goal":{"text":"Clear the three judged findings blocking the gate-provisioning branch"},"name":"orchestrator-gate-fix-findings-2","concurrency":1,"tasks":[{"id":"gate-fix-findings-2","task":"## What\nThe gate-provisioning change on this branch passes every deterministic check — the\npublication gate reports `check: all deterministic checks passed (line coverage\n100.00%)`. It fails the judged tier on three rules, all in the code it adds:\n\n```\nFAIL boundary_inputs_validated\n  scripts/python-install.sh:40: UV_NO_SYNC is consumed by presence alone, so values\n  such as \"0\" or \"false\" silently disable synchronization instead of being parsed or\n  rejected.\nFAIL changed_behavior_has_e2e\n  scripts/python-install.sh:54-55: No end-to-end test verifies the new python-install\n  preserved log's creation, permissions, or secret redaction.\nFAIL comments_earn_their_place\n  scripts/python-install.sh:2-19: The file header is an extended duplicate of the later\n    UV_NO_SYNC, missing-lockfile, and --locked comments rather than a terse file-level\n    purpose.\n  tests/e2e/test_workspace_contract_e2e.py:1032-1043, 1067-1075, 1105-1118: docstrings\n    repeat the historical narrative, the adjacent setup, and implementation detail at\n    excessive length.\n```\n\nClear all three.\n\n**Take the first one seriously — it is a real defect, not a style note.** `UV_NO_SYNC=0`\nand `UV_NO_SYNC=false` currently *disable* provisioning, which is the opposite of what\neither spelling means to a reader. Decide the contract and make the code say it: either\nparse the value and honour falsey spellings, or reject a value you will not honour. Do\nnot leave a switch whose \"off\" setting turns the thing off.\n\nThe second is a genuine coverage gap in this change's own new behaviour: it writes a\npreserved log, and this repository's preserved logs are owner-only and secret-redacted\nby contract. Cover that the way `scripts/preserved-log.sh`'s other callers are covered.\n\nThe third is prose. Cut the header to a terse file-level purpose and let the later\ncomments carry the specifics they already carry; cut the three docstrings to what the\nsetup and assertions do not already say.\n\n## Why\nThis branch is what lets any engine adoption be verified at all — `just gate` currently\ncannot check a change that moves a Python pin, and a four-pin adoption is blocked behind\nit. It is worth landing correctly rather than quickly.\n\nThe `UV_NO_SYNC` finding matters beyond the rule. That variable is the escape hatch the\njourneys use to keep pointing uv at an environment they already control; an escape hatch\nthat fires on `UV_NO_SYNC=0` will eventually be set that way by someone who means the\nopposite, and provisioning will silently not happen. That is the same class of failure\nthis whole branch exists to fix: a step that quietly does not run, and a check that then\nreads whatever was lying around.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `UV_NO_SYNC` has a stated contract and the code implements it. Say which you chose and\n  why, and cover the falsey spellings with a test.\n- The preserved log's creation, permissions, and redaction are covered by an e2e journey.\n  State how you drove it.\n- The four prose sites are cut to what the code and assertions do not already say.\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/main` reports no findings. Report the run id.\n- `just gate` is green. Report it.\n- No `ignore` directive is added and `llmlint.yml` is not edited.\n- Do not move any version pin, and change nothing else on the branch. The provisioning\n  commit is finished work.\n- Another manager's run is working in this repository concurrently in its own worktree;\n  keep documentation edits to what this change requires.\n\n\n## Working conditions on this host — read before your first edit\nAnother manager's run is executing concurrently here and one of its nodes reclaims\npublication workspaces. It has already removed a live dispatch worktree out from under a\nprevious attempt at this exact task, mid-`just check`, losing that attempt's uncommitted\nedits. This is not hypothetical and it is not something you can prevent.\n\nTwo consequences, both binding:\n\n1. **Commit each fix the moment it works, before starting the next one.** Three findings,\n   at least three commits. Do not batch them and commit at the end. A commit is in the\n   branch and survives; a working tree does not.\n2. **If your worktree disappears mid-turn** — `pwd` fails, your session path is gone, git\n   stops resolving — do not investigate it, do not search clones, remotes, or publication\n   checkouts for your commit, and do not try to recover the directory. It was deleted by\n   a process outside this run. Report what you had completed and stop. A previous attempt\n   spent its remaining turns hunting for a directory that no longer existed.\n\nYour branch `onevcs/s-ccff01a9527e` already carries the provisioning change as\n`d1872df0`. That commit is safe regardless of what happens to any worktree.\n","persona":"engineer","max_turns":16,"repo":"/home/nick/projects/ai-orchestrator","base_branch":"onevcs/s-ccff01a9527e","title":"fix(gate): give UV_NO_SYNC a real contract and cover the preserved log","execution_checkout":"ai-orchestrator-isolated"}]},"graph":"/home/nick/projects/ai-orchestrator/graphs/dag-scope.yaml","dir":"/home/nick/projects/ai-orchestrator","heartbeat_interval":1800},"artifacts":[]}
